---
import { href } from '../lib/urls';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../components/cards/Card.astro';
import CaptureDemo from '../components/CaptureDemo.astro';
import ArticleTile from '../components/ArticleTile.astro';
import { card } from '../lib/scopa/deck';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const articles = (await getCollection('articles')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order).slice(0, 3);
---
<BaseLayout title="Learn the Italian card game Scopa" description="Learn the Italian card game your grandparents played. Free interactive Scopa lessons, beautifully illustrated cards, and clear rules for absolute beginners.">
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">An Italian tradition. Your next favorite game.</p><h1>A little tradition.<br />A <em>winning</em> hand.</h1><p class="lede">Learn the Italian card game your grandparents played. Forty cards, a few simple rules, and a seat at the table for everyone.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={href("/learn")}>Learn to Play <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={href("/rules")}>Explore the Rules <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-footnote">Free lessons. No sign-up. A little practice.</p></div>
    <div class="card-stage" role="img" aria-label="Four original Italian playing cards: the seven of coins, ace of cups, king of swords, and three of clubs."><div class="table-oval"></div><div class="card-fan" aria-hidden="true"><Card card={card('clubs', 3)} /><Card card={card('coins', 7)} /><Card card={card('swords', 10)} /><Card card={card('cups', 1)} /></div><div class="card-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><span>Un mazzo</span><strong>40</strong><span>Infinite storie</span></div><span class="stage-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><p class="stage-label" lang="it">Le carte cambiano. La tradizione resta.</p></div>
  </section>
  <div class="intro-strip container"><p>Small deck. Wonderful possibilities.</p><div><strong>40</strong><span>beautiful cards</span></div><div><strong>4</strong><span>traditional suits</span></div><div><strong>11</strong><span>points to win</span></div></div>
  <section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">From “what’s Scopa?” to “one more deal.”</p><h2>Good company.<br />Even better cards.</h2></div><p>Scopa means “sweep” in Italian. Match cards, collect clever combinations, and clear the table. We’ll show you how, one move at a time.</p></div><div class="steps-grid"><article class="step-item"><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Meet your deck.</h3><p>Coins, cups, swords, and clubs. Get to know the forty characters at the heart of the game.</p><span class="small">Lesson one · The essentials</span></article><article class="step-item"><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Make your first capture.</h3><p>A five takes a five. A seven can take a four and a three. Learn when to match, add, or leave a card.</p><span class="small">Lesson two · Hands-on practice</span></article><article class="step-item"><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Count what counts.</h3><p>Discover the settebello, master the score, and find out why sevens are such good company.</p><span class="small">Lesson three · The winning hand</span></article></div></section>
  <section class="green-section section"><div class="container try-grid"><div class="try-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Less reading. More “aha!”</p><h2>The best way to learn?<br />Play a little.</h2><p>Take a seat at our practice table. Short, friendly lessons let you try a move, see why it works, and build the confidence to play with real cards.</p><a class="button button-cream" href={href("/learn")}>Start the interactive lessons <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><CaptureDemo /></div></section>
  <section class="section container cards-feature"><div class="suit-display"><Card card={card('coins', 1)} /><Card card={card('cups', 1)} /><Card card={card('swords', 1)} /><Card card={card('clubs', 1)} /></div><div><p class="eyebrow">A little piece of Italy</p><h2>Not just cards.<br />Little works of art.</h2><p>From the lively Neapolitan pattern to the distinctive Sicilian deck, Italian cards carry their own regional personality. The pictures change. The joy of the game stays.</p><a class="text-link" href={href("/cards")}>Get to know Italian cards <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="section notes-section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Notes from the table</p><h2>A good hand of stories.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={href("/articles")}>All field notes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="article-grid">{articles.map((article, index) => <ArticleTile article={article} index={index} />)}</div></section>
  <section class="closing container"><p class="eyebrow">There’s always room for one more</p><h2>Your seat is waiting.</h2><p>You bring the curiosity. We’ll bring the cards.</p><a class="button" href={href("/learn")}>Let’s learn Scopa <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</BaseLayout>
